<% @title = "Amber design system preview — Amber Framework" %>
<% @meta = "Preview the Amber V2 crystal mark, locally hosted typography, character colors, terminal, personnel cards, and motion rules." %>

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="site-container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Design system · Preview</p>
    <h1>Technical clarity,<br>warmly expressed.</h1>
    <p>This is the working component library for owner proofing. Nothing on this page is approved for production until the visual release gate is signed off.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container brand-grid">
      <article class="brand-card logo-stage reveal">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Primary mark</p>
          <h2>A crystal with a spine.</h2>
          <p>The preview mark is tall, symmetrical, and legible at small sizes. Its facets follow one vertical axis instead of an irregular gemstone silhouette.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="logo-scale-row">
          <img src="/assets/brand/amber-crystal.svg" width="192" height="256" alt="Tall faceted Amber Framework crystal mark">
          <img src="/assets/brand/amber-crystal.svg" width="48" height="64" alt="">
          <img src="/assets/brand/amber-crystal.svg" width="24" height="32" alt="">
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="brand-card type-specimen reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Locally served type</p>
        <p class="display-sample">Build something <em>crystal clear.</em></p>
        <p>Fraunces brings expression and human warmth. Manrope carries the interface. Both variable fonts and their SIL licenses live with the site; the browser never calls a hosted font API.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="brand-card brand-card-wide reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Responsibility colors</p>
        <h2>One crew, clear boundaries.</h2>
        <div class="swatches">
          <div class="swatch" style="background:#fff9ef;">Canvas<br>#FFF9EF</div>
          <div class="swatch" style="background:#f47a16; color:white;">Amber<br>#F47A16</div>
          <div class="swatch" style="background:#147f80; color:white;">Grant<br>#147F80</div>
          <div class="swatch" style="background:#8051a7; color:white;">Gemma<br>#8051A7</div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tinted">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Component shelf</p><h2>Small pieces.<br>One visual language.</h2></div>
        <p>The same border geometry, type, spacing, and state language should carry from marketing pages into documentation.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="component-shelf">
        <article class="component-demo">
          <span class="file-label">Actions</span>
          <div class="component-row"><a class="button button-primary" href="#">Primary action</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="#">Secondary action</a></div>
        </article>
        <article class="component-demo">
          <span class="file-label">Status</span>
          <div class="component-row"><span class="status-badge badge-preview">Preview</span><span class="status-badge badge-supported">V2 beta core</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="component-demo component-demo-wide">
          <span class="file-label">Terminal window</span>
          <div class="terminal mini-terminal"><div class="terminal-toolbar"><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-title">amber — zsh</span></div><div class="terminal-screen"><div><span class="terminal-prompt">$</span> amber new my_app</div><div class="terminal-success">✓ Web application created</div></div></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container motion-spec reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Motion contract</p>
        <h2>Movement must explain state.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Terminal:</strong> progress from install to a running browser.</li>
        <li><strong>Cards:</strong> small pointer depth, never layout movement.</li>
        <li><strong>Crystal field:</strong> decorative response to pointer and scroll.</li>
        <li><strong>Reduced motion:</strong> show the complete state immediately.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
